0..49 Comment "/// This source states flows between large codes."
50..53 Comment "///"
54..98 Comment "/// A large code stores a type in one field."
99..160 Comment "/// The flow type has a level above the universe of the code."
161..235 Comment "/// `Flow[.A = Type[+, 1]](A, B)` is the directed hom of that universe, as"
236..282 Comment "/// Definition 1.2 of the cited work gives it."
283..286 Comment "///"
287..354 Comment "/// The kernel checks each declaration over the level-one universe."
355..413 Comment "/// Each motive decodes its large code at that same level."
414..417 Comment "///"
418..434 Comment "/// - see: #1628"
